<title>UK: UK Dec global trade deficit 845 mln stg.</title>
<headline>UK Dec global trade deficit 845 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics issued the following data on Britain's global trade in December(in million stg, previously announced data in brackets)</p>
<p>    GLOBAL TRADE	     DECEMBER	NOV	 (PREL NOV)</p>
<p>    Trade balance	    -845	   -1,037	  (-959)</p>
<p>    Exports		    13,987	  13,754     (13,877)</p>
<p>    Imports		    14,832	  14,791     (14,836)</p>
<p>    EU trade balance	   -205	    -420	 (-260)</p>
<p>    EU exports		  8,019	   7,753	(7,869)</p>
<p>    EU imports		  8,224	   8,173	(8,129)</p>
<p>    TRADE IN OIL (VALUE MLN STG)	DEC     NOV   (PREL NOV)</p>
<p>    BALANCE				   664     433	(510)</p>
<p>    EXPORTS				 1,114     931    (1,008)</p>
<p>    IMPORTS				   450     498	(498)</p>
<p>Economists had forecast a deficit of 1.1 billion stg.</p>
<p>The ONS said that the whole world goods deficit is narrowing.  </p>
<p>    TRADE VALUE EX OIL/ERRATICS     DEC     NOV    (PREL NOV)</p>
<p>    Trade balance (in mlon stg)    -1,944   -1,657   (-1,664)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports) unch    2.0%	(2.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports) -1.0%   1.0%	(1.5%)</p>
<p>TRADE VOLUME EX OIL/ERRATICS</p>
<p>    Import volume index (base 1990) 132.2   131.4    (130.9)</p>
<p>    Export volume index (base 1990) 139.2   141.4    (141.8)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports) 1.0%    2.5%	(2.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (imps) 9.5%    9.0%	(8.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports) UNCH    2.0%	(2.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (exps) 8.0%    8.0%	(8.0%)</p>
</text>
